Recall also the previous section on clustering.
 There are two slightly different things we might want to do.
 We can reduce the data first and then apply a clustering algorithm to the reduced features.
 Or we can cluster the original data and use a low-dimensional plot to see where the cluster members end up.
 In either case the question is what structure we want the embedding to preserve.
 For example,
 keeping nearby observations together is a different objective from minimizing reconstruction error (as we did in PCA).
\end_layout

