\backslash
mathbf{x}_{i}$ is in a dense region we only need to look a short distance to find about 30 neighbors.
 In a sparse region we need to look further.
 Thus for a fixed perplexity the bandwidth will typically be smaller in dense regions and larger in sparse regions.
\end_layout

